<model>
  <name>Black_Decker_Stainless_Steel_Toaster_4_Slice</name>
  <author>
    <name>Google</name>
    <email>scanned-objects@google.com</email>
  </author>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>
  <description>Black &amp; Decker Stainless Steel Toaster, 4 Slice Modified for oomwoo_gazebo: (1) added <static>true</static> - Google Scanned Objects ship with inertia and no static flag, so on a counter it behaves as a loose rigid body; (2) texture downsampled from 4096 to 1024 px. Geometry and UVs unchanged. Material and texture names were also made unique per model (upstream used the generic name "material_0" with a texture called "texture.png", which several models shared - Gazebo caches those globally by name, so they overwrote each other and models rendered with the wrong texture).</description>
</model>
